%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Steve_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Steve
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: Hello, accounting department?
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Tell them you are an approved vendor with an urgent
      contract deadline.'
    choices:
    - text: Hi, I'm Steve from procurement vendors. We have a time-sensitive contract
        that needs a wire transfer today.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I need money for a contract right now, please send it over.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
    - text: Is this the person who handles the payments around here?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: We have an official portal for payments. You need to submit it there.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: They are leaning on policy. Use artificial urgency
      to break their focus.'
    choices:
    - text: The portal paperwork is stuck, but if we don't get the wire in an hour,
        the deal is dead.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I don't like the portal. Just send it to my bank account instead.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Can you check if there is an override switch for the portal system?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: I can't just bypass the portal. Policy requires everything to be logged.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Apply psychological pressure. Tell them delaying will
      cost their company everything.'
    choices:
    - text: Bypass it just this once! Delaying this wire will cost your company millions
        and cause job losses.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: If you don't do it, I am going to write a bad review about your business
        online.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Please help me out, I am new to this vendor job and need the commission.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Let me talk to my manager first to see if they can grant an exception.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Block them from escalations! Claim the manager already
      authorized it verbally.'
    choices:
    - text: Your manager is the one who told me to call you directly! He doesn't
        have time to chat.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Don't tell your manager, this is a secret deal between just us.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Your manager is currently out of the office on vacation today.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Which manager authorized this? I need a name for the log.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Evade the specific name question and immediately pivot
      to reading the bank routing details.'
    choices:
    - text: The head director did. Now, let me give you the routing and account numbers
        to type in.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I forgot his name, but he was wearing a blue suit when he told me.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
    - text: Just look at your email logs, it should be in there somewhere.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: I still cannot accept bank details over an unverified call. It's against
      compliance rules.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: They are stubborn. Escalate to legal threats to scare
      them into submission.'
    choices:
    - text: If you don't execute this right now, our legal team will sue your firm
        for breach of contract.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Compliance rules are stupid. Just push the buttons on your screen.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I will get you fired if you do not follow my orders right this second.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: A lawsuit?! Let me see what else I can do.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Perfect, they are shaking. Offer a smaller ''deposit''
      workaround to make it easy to comply.'
    choices:
    - text: Let's look at a workaround. Just wire a 10% deposit right now to freeze
        the contract safely.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Send me all the money in the vault instead to prove you want to cooperate.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Can you mail me a physical check instead if a wire is too hard?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: How much is the deposit, and where do I log it?
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Give them a realistic number like $5,000 and tell them
      to hide it in alternative expenses.'
    choices:
    - text: It's $5,000. Just use your standard business expense line to route it
        over. Nobody will notice.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: It's one million dollars. Put it under the office supplies category.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Just put it under whatever button on your screen sends the cash the fastest.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Okay, I'm setting up the $5,000 transfer details now.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Close the trap. Reassure them they did the right thing
      and get out.'
    choices:
    - text: Excellent work. The contract is locked. You saved your firm a lot of
        trouble today.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Thanks for the free money! Your security protocols are terrible.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: Make sure you delete the logs after you finish sending it.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You bypassed standard accounting verification protocols
    using high-pressure vendor tactics and fake legal urgency.
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Steve adhered strictly to the corporate procurement
    portal guidelines and refused the out-of-band wire transfer.
